<.shell title="Breadcrumbs" current={:breadcrumbs}>
  <h1>Breadcrumbs</h1>
  <p class="lead">Where a record's page sits under its section.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <.breadcrumbs>
      <:item label="Members" path="#" />
      <:item label="Avery Chen" />
    </.breadcrumbs>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    On every page below a section's own page, such as a member or an activity, at the top of the <a href={
      page_path(:layout)
    }>page header</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    A section's own page, such as Members. The <a href={page_path(:side_nav)}>side navigation</a>
    shows where you are, and with no link to go back to, the trail renders nothing.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      It starts at the section and names each level down. The top bar names the team, so the trail leaves it out.
    </li>
    <li>The last item is the current page and is not a link.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.breadcrumbs&gt;</code>
    with an <code>&lt;:item label="…" path=&#123;…&#125; /&gt;</code>
    for each level.
  </p>
</.shell>
